    "text": "To determine how many seeds Bob can plant in each row, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the length of the row from feet to inches.\n2. Divide the length of the row in inches by the space each seed needs.\n\nFirst, we know that 1 foot is equal to 12 inches. Therefore, the length of the row in inches is:\n\\[ 120 \\text{ feet} \\times 12 \\text{ inches/foot} = 1440 \\text{ inches} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine how many seeds can fit into this 1440-inch length, given that each seed needs 18 inches of space. We do this by dividing the total length of the row by the space each seed needs:\n\\[ 1440 \\text{ inches} \\div 18 \\text{ inches/seed} = 80 \\text{ seeds} \\]\n\nSo, the number of seeds Bob can plant in each row is \\(\\boxed{80}\\).",
